#!/bin/bash
# Test double for /bin/launchctl (B-0c kyctl tests). Simulates bootstrap / kickstart / print /
# bootout for a gui/<uid> domain inside $FAKE_LAUNCHCTL_DIR and records every call. bash 3.2.
#   calls.log            one line per invocation (the argv)
#   loaded/<label>       the service is bootstrapped
#   pid/<label>          pid of the simulated job (a background sleep) while "running"
# Markers:  no_run (bootstrap/kickstart load but start nothing) · bootout_stuck (bootout
#           leaves the service loaded) · claim_running/<label> (print claims "running" with the
#           pid in pid/<label> whether or not it is alive) · print_garbage (print emits noise)
set -u
S="${FAKE_LAUNCHCTL_DIR:?FAKE_LAUNCHCTL_DIR is required}"
mkdir -p "$S/loaded" "$S/pid" "$S/claim_running"
printf '%s\n' "$*" >> "$S/calls.log"
cmd="${1:-}"; shift || true
label_of() { local t="$1"; echo "${t##*/}"; }
alive() { [ -s "$S/pid/$1" ] && kill -0 "$(cat "$S/pid/$1")" 2>/dev/null; }
spawn() {
  [ -e "$S/no_run" ] && return 0
  alive "$1" && return 0
  /bin/sleep 600 >/dev/null 2>&1 &
  echo "$!" > "$S/pid/$1"
}
case "$cmd" in
  bootstrap)
    plist="${2:?}"; label="$(basename "$plist" .plist)"
    if [ -e "$S/loaded/$label" ]; then echo "Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error" >&2; exit 5; fi
    [ -f "$plist" ] || { echo "Bootstrap failed: 2: No such file or directory" >&2; exit 2; }
    : > "$S/loaded/$label"; spawn "$label"; exit 0 ;;
  kickstart)
    [ "${1:-}" = "-k" ] && shift
    label="$(label_of "${1:?}")"
    [ -e "$S/loaded/$label" ] || { echo "Could not find service \"$label\" in domain for uid" >&2; exit 113; }
    spawn "$label"; exit 0 ;;
  print)
    label="$(label_of "${1:?}")"
    if [ -e "$S/print_garbage" ]; then echo "?? unexpected launchctl output ??"; exit 0; fi
    [ -e "$S/loaded/$label" ] || { echo "Could not find service \"$label\" in domain for uid" >&2; exit 113; }
    echo "$1 = {"
    echo "	active count = 1"
    echo "	type = LaunchAgent"
    if alive "$label" || [ -e "$S/claim_running/$label" ]; then
      echo "	state = running"
      echo "	pid = $(cat "$S/pid/$label" 2>/dev/null)"
    else
      echo "	state = not running"
    fi
    echo "	last exit code = $(cat "$S/last_exit.$label" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
    echo "}"
    exit 0 ;;
  bootout)
    label="$(label_of "${1:?}")"
    [ -e "$S/loaded/$label" ] || { echo "Boot-out failed: 3: No such process" >&2; exit 3; }
    [ -e "$S/bootout_stuck" ] && exit 0
    if alive "$label"; then kill "$(cat "$S/pid/$label")" 2>/dev/null; fi
    rm -f "$S/pid/$label" "$S/loaded/$label"; exit 0 ;;
  *) echo "fake_launchctl: unsupported subcommand: $cmd" >&2; exit 64 ;;
esac
